---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Privacy Notice · SoyaOS Developer Portal">
  <article class="prose prose-stone max-w-3xl">
    <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-soya-accent">v0.2.0 Stable</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Privacy notice</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-6 text-soya-ink/70">
      Effective August 20, 2026. This notice describes the limited data used by
      the free SoyaOS Cloud v0.2.0 service.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">What SoyaOS keeps</h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-6 text-soya-ink/70">
      <li>Your GitHub numeric user ID, login, display name and encrypted Portal session.</li>
      <li>API Key identifiers, prefixes and one-way HMAC digests. Raw keys are shown once.</li>
      <li>For 24 hours: request ID, tenant and Key IDs, model, timestamps, latency, status, token counts and normalized error code.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">Inference content</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-soya-ink/70">
      Prompts and generated responses are sent to Cloudflare Workers AI to
      perform inference. SoyaOS does not persist those bodies in D1 or request
      traces. Do not submit secrets, regulated data or content that requires a
      guaranteed residency region.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">Location and deletion</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-soya-ink/70">
      The control-data primary currently runs in Cloudflare&apos;s Western North
      America region (WNAM). Requests may be processed on Cloudflare&apos;s managed
      network; the service makes no data-residency commitment. Trace metadata
      expires after 24 hours. You can revoke keys at any time; account deletion
      requests can be filed in the public developer-portal repository.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-8 text-xs text-soya-ink/50">
      This service is not intended for sensitive or production-regulated workloads.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
